   Project 21: Olympics Medal Analysis
      Build a data analysis project that processes historical Olympic data to uncover patterns in country performance and medal distribution over time.
      Key Skills: 
         Data loading and cleaning with Pandas, statistical analysis with NumPy,    simple plots using Matplotlib, data aggregation.
      Features:
         Load and clean Olympics dataset (from Kaggle).
         Handle missing values and clean country names.
         Compute total medal tallies, most successful countries, and medals by year.
      Visualize:
         Top 10 countries by gold, silver, bronze, and total medals.
         Medal trends over years.
         Use NumPy to compute average and standard deviation of medals per event or country.

   Project 22: Stock Market Technical Analysis
      Develop a tool to analyze stock data and compute technical indicators to identify price patterns and potential trading signals.
      Key Skills: 
         Time series analysis with Pandas, rolling statistics with NumPy, financial plotting with Matplotlib, signal detection with SciPy.
      Features:
         Load stock market data from CSV (e.g., Yahoo Finance).
         Calculate indicators such as:
            Simple and Exponential Moving Averages (SMA, EMA)
            Bollinger Bands
            Daily returns
      Visualize:
         Price with overlaid technical indicators
         Peaks in price using scipy.signal.find_peaks
      Apply smoothing and noise reduction to better identify trends.

   Project 23: Human Activity Recognition using Signal Processing
      Analyze and classify smartphone sensor data to identify different human activities like walking, sitting, or running.
      Key Skills:
         Time-series segmentation with Pandas, signal feature extraction with NumPy, FFT and filters with SciPy, advanced visualizations.
      Features:
         Load accelerometer and gyroscope data from the UCI HAR dataset.
         Segment data into windows and extract statistical and signal-based features:
            Mean, standard deviation, energy, entropy
            Frequency domain features using FFT
      Visualize:
         Sensor signals over time
         Frequency spectrum
         Activity distributions
      Bonus: 
         Train a simple classifier (e.g., logistic regression or decision tree) using Scikit-learn to classify activities based on extracted features.

   Project 24: Iris Flower Classification
      Classify the species of an Iris flower based on petal and sepal measurements using a simple machine learning model.
      Key Skills: 
         Scikit-learn built-in datasets, KNN and Logistic Regression, evaluation metrics, exploratory data analysis.
      Features:
         Load the Iris dataset using sklearn.datasets.load_iris.
         Explore the dataset: dimensions, feature distribution, correlations.
         Train models like K-Nearest Neighbors or Logistic Regression.
         Evaluate performance using accuracy_score, confusion_matrix, and classification_report.
         Visualize decision boundaries using two selected features.
   
   Project 25: Movie Review Sentiment Analysis (NLP)
      Build a sentiment classifier that predicts whether a movie review is positive or negative using machine learning and NLP.
      Key Skills: 
         Natural Language Processing, text vectorization, Scikit-learn pipelines, Naive Bayes and Logistic Regression, hyperparameter tuning.
      Features:
         Load IMDB dataset using nltk or a Kaggle source.
         Preprocess text: lowercase, remove punctuation, stopword removal.
         Use TfidfVectorizer to convert text into numerical features.
         Train a Naive Bayes and Logistic Regression classifier.
         Tune model with GridSearchCV and test performance.
         Evaluate using precision, recall, F1-score, and confusion matrix.

   Project 26: House Price Prediction – Regression Pipeline
      Create a full pipeline that processes real estate data and predicts house prices using regression models and feature engineering.
      Key Skills: 
         Scikit-learn Pipelines, ColumnTransformer, regression modeling, data preprocessing, feature selection, model tuning.
      Features:
         Load Ames Housing dataset from Kaggle.
         Handle missing values, encode categorical features, scale numeric ones.
         Build a Pipeline with ColumnTransformer for preprocessing.
         Train multiple regression models: Linear Regression, Ridge, Random Forest, Gradient Boosting.
         Evaluate using RMSE and R² score.
         Perform model selection and tuning using GridSearchCV and cross_val_score.
